  "reason": "With no completed experiments, all design decisions are uncertain. The most informative first experiment is a minimal, well-understood baseline that establishes a performance floor for all subsequent comparisons. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) uses the simplest profile setting and the most standard, interpretable RNA encoder (PCA), isolating the contribution of RNA data alone without confounding from image modality, learned encoders, or multi-profile aggregation. This baseline will let me quantify how much additional value each design axis (image modality, learned encoders, multiprofile aggregation, multimodal fusion) contributes in later experiments. Starting from the simplest configuration maximizes interpretability of every future delta and is the most efficient use of the first experiment under a limited budget."
}

